// A parameter that nothing reads still gets a register (ZYVM-030, 2026-10-17).
//
// The VM's compiler recounted a function's registers from the instructions
// that survived dead-code elimination, and a parameter nothing reads is in none
// of them: `f(a, b, c) { <~ a }` got a frame of one register, and every call
// wrote `b` and `c` past its end, without a bounds check. A release build
// answered right by luck; a debug build aborts. What holds it is the compiler
// test `a_frame_holds_every_parameter_even_one_nothing_reads`; this file is
// the program, for whoever runs the corpus on a debug build.
f(a, b, c) {
    <~ a
}
t = 0
@ i:1..5 { t = t + f(i, i, i) }
>> t ¶

g = (x, y) -> x
>> g(7, 8) ¶
